  "519": {
    "hero_name": "Ao'yin",
    "skills": [
      {
        "skill_name": "Passive Skill: Hidden Dragon",
        "cd": null,
        "mana_cost": null,
        "tags": [
          "Enhance",
          "Damage"
        ],
        "description": "The elemental Dragon Souls from Ao'yin's last 2 skill attacks will be attached to his primary and secondary swords. He deals 165 (100%) physical damage with his primary sword, and if there are other enemies nearby he will also attack them with his secondary sword to deal 57 (35% - 70%) physical damage.\nWhen using skills, he gains 1 Dragon Soul mark (up to 3 marks) and 1 enhanced Basic Attack. Using the enhanced Basic Attack expends all marks, unleashing Dragon Souls that attack the target (Each mark grants 1 extra attack, with subsequent hits dealing half damage). Effects vary depending on the type of Dragon Soul attached to his primary sword.\nWhen switching between elements, Dragon Souls of the same element is prioritized."
      },
      {
        "skill_name": "Skill 1: Flaming Palm",
        "cd": "12.5s",
        "mana_cost": "60",
        "tags": [
          "Damage",
          "Damage"
        ],
        "description": "Ao'yin unleashes a wave of sword energy, gaining 1 extra Dragon Soul mark and dealing 270 (270 + 70% extra) physical damage and 70 (70 + 16% extra) true damage (and 50% splash damage behind the target) to up to 3 targets within range.\nUse of Flaming Palm attaches 1 Fire Dragon Soul to his sword, allowing him to deal an extra 15 physical damage during Basic Attacks. If a Fire Dragon Soul is attached to both swords, he deals 50% more damage. If a Fire Dragon Soul is attached to his primary sword, the first strike of his enhanced Basic Attack will deal 97 (48 + 30%) true damage while the subsequent two strikes will deal an equal amount of physical damage.\nSkill use speed scales with Attack Speed."
      },
      {
        "skill_name": "Skill 2: Downpour",
        "cd": "12.5s",
        "mana_cost": "60",
        "tags": [
          "Recover",
          "Damage"
        ],
        "description": "Ao'yin unleashes sword energy, dealing 180 (180 + 45% extra) physical damage to up to 3 targets within range (dealing 50% splash damage behind the targets), and recovering 150 (150 + 2.5% extra) Health upon hit.\nUse of Downpour attaches 1 Water Dragon Soul to his sword, allowing him to recover 18 Health and 0.5% Mana from Basic Attacks. If a Water Dragon Soul is attached to both swords, he recovers 50% more. If a Water Dragon Soul is attached to his primary sword, his enhanced Basic Attacks will deal 97 (48 + 30%) physical damage each strike, for a total of 3 strikes. Landing a hit on the enemy recovers 150 (150 + 2.5% extra) Health.\nRecovery effects are halved against non-hero units. Skill use speed scales with Attack Speed."
      },
      {
        "skill_name": "Skill 3: Riding the Wind",
        "cd": "12.5s",
        "mana_cost": "60",
        "tags": [
          "Crowd Control",
          "Speed Up",
          "Damage"
        ],
        "description": "Ao'yin unleashes a wave of sword energy, gaining 30% Movement Speed (diminishes over time). He also deals 180 (180 + 45% extra) physical damage (with 50% splash damage) to up to 3 targets within range and knocks them back.\nUse of Riding the Wind attaches 1 Wind Dragon Soul to his sword, granting him 16 Movement Speed. If a Wind Dragon Soul is attached to both swords, he gains an extra 50% Movement Speed. If a Wind Dragon Soul is attached to his primary sword, he will deal 97 (48 + 30%) physical damage and knock back the enemy with every strike of his enhanced Basic Attack, for a total of 3 strikes.\nSkill use speed scales with Attack Speed."
      },
      {
        "skill_name": "Skill 4: Infinite Vastness",
        "cd": "80s",
        "mana_cost": "120",
        "tags": [
          "Enhance",
          "Crowd Control",
          "Damage"
        ],
        "description": "Ao'yin reveals his true white dragon form and soars into the sky for up to 4.5s, then dives forward. During this time, he is untargetable and ignores terrain, but cannot attack. He deals 400 (400 + 80% extra) physical damage to enemies in his path and slows them by 15%.\nUpon landing, he deals the same amount of physical damage and applies Dread to nearby enemies for 1s. Targets afflicted with Dread will involuntarily move away from Ao'yin.\nAo'yin then unsheathes his True Dragon Sword, gaining 20% AS and 25 Attack Range, and the ability to attack up to two additional targets for 10s.\nAo'yin can switch his swords' elemental Dragon Souls while in flight.\nFlight speed increases with his Ultimate's level."
      }
    ],
