          "Movement"
        ],
        "description": "Umbrosa dashes forward, knocking back enemies in her path (not considered a crowd control effect) and dealing 150 (150 + 50% extra physical attack) physical damage. At the same time, she triggers the Featherblade marks of all hit targets and spreads them to nearby enemies.\nIf there are enemies ahead, Umbrosa performs a graceful dance, throwing flying blades that strike 8 times, each dealing 110 (110 + 38% extra physical attack) physical damage and recovering 45 (45 + 0.8% extra Health) Health (healing is halved when hitting non-hero units). If Umbrosa is in the Indomitable state, the final strike deals an extra 100% damage. Each hit consumes 1 stack of the target's marks, dealing an extra 40 (40 + 15% extra physical attack) physical damage.\nShe can move freely while dancing, and using the skill again will cancel its effects. If the dance is not triggered, the skill's cooldown will be reduced to 60% of the original."
      },
      {
        "skill_name": "Final Frenzy",
        "cd": "55s",
        "mana_cost": "100",
        "tags": [
          "Indomitable",
          "Enhance",
          "Damage"
        ],
        "description": "Umbrosa reignites her former glory as an Austren, dealing 400 (400 + 140% extra physical attack) physical damage to nearby enemies while gaining 50% temporary Health and 50% Movement Speed that diminishes over time. She also enters the Indomitable state for 4s. Any recovery effects will be tallied only after the state ends.\nIf Umbrosa is defeated while this skill is not on cooldown, she will resurrect after a short delay. Upon resurrecting, she will deal 400 (400 + 140% extra physical attack) physical damage to nearby enemies, and this skill will enter cooldown.\nPassive: When leveling up this skill, Feathered Tempest gains an additional 2 strikes of damage, while her melee Basic Attack gains an additional 1 strike of damage. Additional strikes deal 50 physical damage each.\nIf her temporary Health is expended, she will immediately exit the Indomitable state. When she resurrects, she only gains 50% of the Health she would have gained if the skill were actively used."
      }
    ],
